@startuml
title UC-04 - Inspect and Register Connection
actor "Platform Engineer / Admin" as PE
boundary ConnectionController as API
control ConnectionService as Service
control KubeconfigParser as Parser
boundary KubernetesConnectionVerifier as K8s
boundary AWSConnectionVerifier as AWS
boundary ConnectionCredentialStore as Secrets
database ConnectionRepository as Repo
PE -> API: Inspect kubeconfig [MS-01..03, VAR-01]
API -> Service: InspectKubeconfig(org, document)
Service -> Parser: Parse supported contexts
Parser --> Service: safe context/cluster/endpoint metadata
Service --> API: metadata only (no write/network)
API --> PE: select context + review destination
PE -> API: Check and save [MS-04]
alt Kubernetes [VAR-01, first delivery]
  API -> Service: RegisterKubeconfig(org, name, document, context)
  Service -> Parser: Revalidate + normalize selected context
  Parser --> Service: selected config (request memory)
  Service -> K8s: Verify(config), no resource creation [MS-05]
  K8s --> Service: safe VerificationResult
else AWS [VAR-02, v2 required]
  API -> Service: RegisterAWSDriverAccount(org, command)
  Service -> AWS: Verify(identity, regions, provisioning capabilities), no resource creation
  AWS --> Service: safe VerificationResult
end
Service -> Service: Generate unique key from name
Service -> Secrets: Put(org, key, immutable attempt, credential) [MS-06]
Secrets --> Service: opaque reference
Service -> Repo: CreateConnection(READY) <<transaction>> [MS-07]
alt Insert succeeds
  Repo --> Service: committed Connection
  Service --> API: public metadata DTO [MS-08..09]
  API --> PE: Registered; clear credential; reload list
else Insert fails
  Repo --> Service: failure
  Service -> Secrets: Delete only own attempt (bounded cleanup)
  Service --> API: safe failure; report cleanup error if any
  API --> PE: Registration failed
end
note right of Repo
No overwrite on collision/concurrency.
Organization default is unchanged.
No secret bytes in logical state.
end note
PE -> API: Register Secret Store Connection [SS-01..06]
API -> Service: Role/org-gated Vault register command
Service -> Service: Verify KV v2/capabilities, cleanup own probe
Service -> Secrets: Put scoped immutable store token
Service -> Repo: Insert separate SecretStoreConnection READY
Service --> PE: Safe metadata, never token/ref
boundary ComposeBootstrap as Bootstrap
Bootstrap -> Service: Ensure managed platform-vault [SS-07..08]
Service -> Service: Shared validation + Vault verifier + probe cleanup
Service -> Secrets: Read existing scoped credential / Put own replacement
Service -> Repo: CAS admit matching identity <<transaction>>
note right of Repo
Preserve ID/key/endpoints and Environment references.
Create ordinary store or refresh marked managed credential.
No legacy conversion/backfill or global token fallback.
Concurrent loser never cleans winner credential.
end note
alt Admission fails
  Service -> Secrets: Delete only own attempt credential
  Service --> Bootstrap: Safe failure; stop backend startup
else Admitted or unchanged
  Service --> Bootstrap: Ordinary verified store; runtime resolves credential ref
end
== V01 account management [AC-01..12] ==
PE -> API: View / rename / verify / replace (expected version)
API -> Service: Scoped PE/Admin account command
Service -> Repo: Get account by Organization and key
alt Metadata rename
  Service -> Service: Validate name; preserve target/ref
else Reverify or same-target credential replacement
  Service -> Secrets: Resolve stored credential privately (verify only)
  Service -> K8s: Read-only verify Internal credential (or AWS verifier)
  Service -> Service: Preserve target identity; reject redirection
  opt Replacement only
    Service -> Secrets: Put new immutable attempt object
    Secrets --> Service: new private reference
  end
end
Service -> Repo: CAS metadata/ref/verification/version <<transaction>>
alt CAS succeeds
  Service --> API: Safe account DTO with new version
  API --> PE: Success; clear credential; refresh
else Stale or failure
  opt Own new attempt exists
    Service -> Secrets: Delete only uncommitted own attempt
  end
  API --> PE: Safe failure / stale; reload before retry
end
note right of Secrets
Keep previously committed objects for pinned targets.
Account types AWS/INTERNAL; no Environment assignment.
AWS probe regions are evidence, not applicability.
end note
== EC2 role account [EC2-01..05] ==
boundary EC2RoleProvider as EC2
PE -> API: Register EC2 role (name, expected role ARN, regions)
API -> Service: RegisterEC2Role(org, command)
Service -> EC2: IMDSv2 + STS + GetRole; region/capability checks
EC2 --> Service: Safe role ARN/RoleId/account verification
Service -> Repo: CreateConnection AWS_EC2_ROLE (no secret ref)
Service --> API: Safe Account DTO
API --> PE: Verified account
note right of EC2
Explicit source only, no host chain fallback.
Reverify uses version CAS and same role identity.
Terraform refresh uses authenticated private loopback endpoint.
end note
@enduml
